Package: kmod-keys-encrypted
Version: 6.6.73-r1
Depends: kernel (=6.6.73~6afc42d253ef3d8182922d815ccb143d-r1), kmod-crypto-cbc, kmod-crypto-hmac, kmod-crypto-rng, kmod-crypto-sha256, kmod-keys-trusted
Source: feeds/base/kernel/linux
SourceName: kernel
License: GPL-2.0-only
LicenseFiles: COPYING
Section: kernel
SourceDateEpoch: 1738624177
Architecture: arm_cortex-a7_neon-vfpv4
Installed-Size: 30720
Filename: kmod-keys-encrypted_6.6.73-r1_arm_cortex-a7_neon-vfpv4.ipk
Size: 8961
SHA256sum: a4c57f4e6bb8955f462293c82783ea57e6e0706ce5896839f3760f0548f1480a
Description:  This module provides support for create/encrypting/decrypting keys
 in the kernel.  Encrypted keys are kernel generated random numbers,
 which are encrypted/decrypted with a 'master' symmetric key. The
 'master' key can be either a trusted-key or user-key type.
 Userspace only ever sees/stores encrypted blobs.

Package: kmod-keys-trusted
Version: 6.6.73-r1
Depends: kernel (=6.6.73~6afc42d253ef3d8182922d815ccb143d-r1), kmod-crypto-hash, kmod-crypto-hmac, kmod-crypto-sha1, kmod-tpm
